  "e.relax": "β<sub>0</sub> under-relaxation",
  "e.couple_note": "★<strong>The free-boundary equilibrium is re-solved every K steps</strong>, the metric re-traced, and dV′/dt carried across the join (the state arrived on the old metric; the first step on the new one consumes that volume change, or energy appears out of nothing). ★★<strong>The feedback is a SHAPE feedback, not only an amplitude</strong>: the solver's source is j<sub>φ</sub> = j<sub>c</sub>[β₀R/R₀+(1−β₀)R₀/R](1−ψ̄<sup>emp</sup>)<sup>enp</sup>, whose shape factor <strong>is</strong> dp/dψ̄ normalised — so it is fitted to the pressure gradient the march produced, and β₀ is moved by the ratio of two β<sub>p</sub> (the transport one against the last equilibrium's), under-relaxed. Both, and the fit residual, are reported per round. ★It is still a <strong>two-parameter family</strong>: a shape it cannot reach shows up in that residual.",
  "e.couple_note_off": "★Coupling is available on the device-equilibrium geometry only: re-solving needs a set of coil currents. On the imported-g-file and Miller tiers the geometry is <strong>frozen</strong> for the whole march.",

  "e.scope": "★<strong>This bar solves the time-dependent core transport system</strong>: the heat channels (3/2)∂(V′nT)/∂t + ∂q/∂ρ = V′Q with q = −V′⟨|∇ρ|²⟩nχ∂T/∂ρ, the particle channel in the same form, and the current channel as upstream's standardised psi diffusion. ρ is <strong>ρ<sub>tor</sub> [m]</strong>, V′ = dV/dρ [m²], T in eV, sources in W/m³ — that unit consistency is the substantive difference from the bar above.",
  "e.caveat": "<strong>Offline tier</strong>: you press the key and watch it run. ★<strong>The sawtooth is a trigger plus mixing, not a stability theory</strong>: switchable on with the current channel — after each step, if q crosses 1, the profiles are flattened inside r<sub>mix</sub> = k·r<sub>q=1</sub> conserving <em>∫V′y dρ</em> and psi is rebuilt there from q = 1 (the kernel's <code>q_crossing</code> + <code>sawtooth_crash</code>). ★k <strong>has no default</strong> (reduced models take 1 to 1.4), so it is a control. ★The step after a crash carries <strong>no Ohmic power</strong>: reconnection moves psi by an amount no resistive step took, and sigma E² on it would report a spike that never happened. ★<strong>Not here yet</strong>: a pedestal model, a turbulent closure (TGLF is on the 1.5-D bar; here there is a constant tier and a neoclassical one), multiple ions and impurity <strong>transport</strong> (an impurity enters the radiation only; it has no channel of its own here), the momentum channel, the SOL and the targets. ★<strong>Prescribed rather than solved</strong>: the χ<sub>e</sub>/χ<sub>i</sub> ratio, D<sub>n</sub>/χ<sub>e</sub>, the pinch, the deposition shapes, the driven-current shape and the composition (one thermal deuterium species, the impurity concentration a prescribed constant; Z<sub>eff</sub> enters the resistivity, the bremsstrahlung and the bootstrap and <strong>not</strong> quasi-neutrality).",
