  "e.fm.otol": "Outer-loop convergence (relative change of the pressure and current profiles)",
  "e.fm_outer_note": "★★<strong>The outer loop is not a new mechanism added to this tier — it is the Picard split already running.</strong> Inside the match the burn is already <strong>frozen at each iteration boundary</strong> and the pedestal is already <strong>lagged by one</strong>, and the reason was measured: with the alpha power live inside the Newton Jacobian, one probe moves every radius of a channel together, so the core temperature rises, the alpha power rises, and <strong>the target chases its own answer</strong> until the Newton step points the wrong way. All the outer loop does is <strong>wrap three more things in that same Picard</strong>: the <strong>steady current</strong> (the psi channel driven to steady state on the matched profiles, bootstrap from Redl, Ohmic through sigma_neo, giving a new q), the <strong>sawtooth</strong> (rebuilt when q(0) falls below 1), and the <strong>equilibrium</strong> (free boundary re-solved on the new pressure and current, metric ladder rebuilt). ★<strong>The convergence test is upstream's own</strong>: the relative change of the pressure and current profiles, 5 % by default. ★<strong>One round is exactly today's behaviour</strong> (match only, no alternation), so every existing case runs unchanged. ★<strong>The coupling cadence K stays refused on this tier</strong>: it counts STEPS, and this tier has no time axis.",
  "e.fm_note": "★★<strong>This tier does not march, it solves.</strong> The other three answer「what happens if I advance with this chi」; this one answers <strong>「which gradients make the model flux equal the flux the sources require」</strong> — the unknowns are <strong>a/L<sub>Te</sub> and a/L<sub>Ti</sub></strong> at each match radius (two channels, laid out channel-fastest as the kernel's Jacobian expects), the model flux is <code>gm3·n·chi·z·T</code> with chi from the neoclassical floor plus TGLF (the SAME closure the turbulent tier runs), and the target is the volume integral of the sources inside the surface, per unit V'. <strong>The electron-ion exchange enters the two targets with opposite signs</strong> (the kernel's own convention, q<sub>e</sub>−s<sub>x</sub> and q<sub>i</sub>+s<sub>x</sub>, positive to the ions), so the split between the channels is solved for as well. ★<strong>The Newton machine is the kernel's</strong> (<code>flux_match</code>, six ABI entries, held against TGYRO's own iteration table to 1e-6): which point to probe, how the Jacobian is assembled, the clamp, the per-point backoff and the convergence test are all on that side; this side supplies only the flux model, because a callback cannot cross the ABI. ★<strong>The Jacobian costs one extra flux evaluation per CHANNEL</strong>, not per unknown — one probe moves <strong>every radius of a channel together</strong>, which is exact for a radially decoupled local model. ★<strong>The match radii ARE the TGLF radii</strong> (求值半径数 above) rather than a fifth control: matching where the closure was never evaluated would be matching an interpolation. ★<strong>A match that will not converge is reported as a failure</strong>, naming which criterion was missed and which radius and channel carried the worst residual — it <strong>never falls back to a constant chi</strong>.",
  "e.fm.replaces": "★<strong>The flux-match tier has no time axis</strong>: it is a root find for the steady state, not a march to it. So the time step, the step count, the adaptive target, the waveform, the continuation, the density / current / momentum channels, the sawtooth and the equilibrium alternation are all <strong>disabled</strong> rather than quietly ignored — and the heat channel is forced on, because it is the pair being matched. ★<strong>The alternation belongs elsewhere</strong>: iterating the equilibrium AROUND this solve is the self-consistent stationary outer loop, which is a different thing.",
  "e.fm.out": "Flux match",
  "e.fm.hist": "Residual per iteration",
  "e.fm.radii": "Per match radius",
  "e.fm.col.it": "iter",
  "e.fm.col.res": "max |Q<sub>model</sub>/Q<sub>target</sub> − 1|",
  "e.fm.col.tped": "T<sub>ped</sub> [keV]",
  "e.fm.col.rho": "ρ̂",
  "e.fm.col.alt": "a/L<sub>Te</sub> · a/L<sub>Ti</sub>",
  "e.fm.col.qe": "Q<sub>e</sub> model/target [kW/m²]",
  "e.fm.col.qi": "Q<sub>i</sub> model/target [kW/m²]",
  "e.fm.out_note": "★<strong>Two tables, not one number.</strong>「It converged」 is a claim about a <strong>sequence</strong> and a single final value cannot support it; and a max residual that passed hides which radius was carrying it. ★The residual column is <strong>dimensionless</strong>: the kernel's residual is (f−g)² in W²/m⁴, and this side rescales it by a <strong>per-point weight</strong> into a relative flux difference before taking the square root. <strong>Scaling each point consistently changes nothing the matcher decides</strong> (W cancels in (W J<sub>f</sub> − W J<sub>g</sub>)dx = −W(f−g)r, and the per-point backoff compares each point with itself), so this is a change of <strong>measure and not of algorithm</strong>; the weights are <strong>frozen</strong> at the starting target, or「the residual fell each round」 would be a statement about the yardstick. ★<strong>The T<sub>ped</sub> column</strong> carries numbers only with the pedestal model on: EPED1-NN takes the global β<sub>N</sub>, which is what this solve is producing, so it is re-evaluated at each iteration boundary on the <strong>previous</strong> iteration's profiles — the same one-step lag the marching tiers carry.",
  "e.fm.burn": "★<strong>The burn is frozen at the point each iteration starts from</strong> (a Picard split: Newton in the conduction, Picard in the burn) — with the alpha power inside the Jacobian the ITER case climbed rather than fell over twelve iterations and the innermost matched a/L<sub>Ti</sub> was driven negative (a hollow profile): a probe raises <strong>every radius of a channel together</strong>, so the core temperature rises, the alpha power with it, and <strong>the target chases its own answer</strong>. ★What the freeze costs is measured: the same residual re-taken at the matched point with the alpha power live differs by <strong>{d} %</strong>. ★Closing that feedback is the self-consistent stationary outer loop's job, not this tier's.",
